\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Who fathoms the eternal thought?
\par Who talks of scheme and plan?
\par The Lord is God! He needeth not
\par The poor device of man.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Here in the madenning maze  of things,
\par When tossed by storm and flood,
\par To one fixed ground my spirit clings;
\par I know that God good!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I long for household voices gone,
\par For vanished smiles I long;
\par But God hath led my dear ones on,
\par And He can do no wrong.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I know not what the future hath
\par Of marvel or suprise,
\par Assured alone that life and death
\par His mercy underlies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And if my heart and flesh are weak
\par To bear an untried pain
\par The bruised breed He will not break 
\par But strenghten and sustain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. No offering of my own I have,
\par Nor works my faith to prove;
\par I can but give the gift He gave,
\par And plead His love for love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. And so beside the silent sea
\par Awaits the muffled oar;
\par No harm from Him can come to me
\par On ocean or on shore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. I know not where His islands lift
\par Their fronded palms in air;
\par I only know I cannot drift
\par Beyond His love and care.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

